    <briefdescription>
<para>Documentation for compile-time configuration macros. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The DOXYGEN_DOCS macro is used exclusively by documentation generators like Doxygen. Because minipaxtar enables reading and writing by default, these option macros (such as <ref refid="group__mptar__stable__config_1gac16c82dbd512401c9f34972f46f78729" kindref="member">MPTAR_NO_READ</ref>) are not normally defined in the source code. Wrapping them in &quot;#ifdef DOXYGEN_DOCS&quot; allows Doxygen to index and document them without altering actual build configurations.</para>
<para>Stable configuration macros and custom conversion/string hooks.</para>
<para>These options, features, and custom conversion hooks are guaranteed stable and will follow standard deprecation cycles if ever slated for modification or removal.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Default Implementations</title><para>When a stable function override is not explicitly defined, minipaxtar may map it to the corresponding standard C library function when the library is available and supported. For example, <ref refid="group__mptar__stable__config_1ga111bc8b972f65d7b004e696d2675c19c" kindref="member">mptar_strlen</ref> maps to <computeroutput>strlen</computeroutput> when neither <ref refid="group__mptar__stable__config_1ga111bc8b972f65d7b004e696d2675c19c" kindref="member">mptar_strlen</ref> nor the legacy <ref refid="group__mptar__stable__config_1ga8f59b4a2c5cfd6fcc0d5436c0f94d2ae" kindref="member">MPTAR_CUSTOM_STRLEN</ref> is defined. When <ref refid="group__mptar__stable__config_1ga4c45a5dd495ad2a7ebd5f51c2e7effe5" kindref="member">MPTAR_NO_STD</ref> is defined the functions are mapped to the built-in nostd replacements, by default it is defined unless <ref refid="group__mptar__stable__config_1ga6f1f06dee6bb98cd553e1edb542d710e" kindref="member">MPTAR_USE_STD</ref> is defined.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Custom function hooks can now be provided directly by defining the exact function name macro (e.g., #define mptar_strlen my_strlen). The legacy <computeroutput>MPTAR_CUSTOM_*</computeroutput> macros are deprecated but remain supported for backward compatibility. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
